codex
The regenerated `.mpy` is byte-identical. Value-level differential testing covered 5,380 cases with zero value or input-mutation mismatches; it did expose a real but non-value difference: for empty and singleton inputs, `solution.py` returns the original list object while the canonical implementation returns a fresh list. I’ll account for that aliasing boundary in adequacy rather than letting finite tests stand in for the proof. Fresh K compilation and proof execution are next.
exec
/bin/bash -lc 'chmod +x /audit-output/evidence/run_stage3.sh
/audit-output/evidence/run_stage3.sh
runner_status=$?
printf '"'stage3_runner_exit=%d\\n' \""'$runner_status"
tail -n 260 /audit-output/evidence/stage3-reconstruction.log' in /audit-output
